                                                    "desc:8":  "§cREAD THIS BEFORE IT READS YOU§r\n  §1SCRAM§r at 8,000 core heat - the plant slams shut.\n  §cMELTDOWN§r at 10,000 - a vertical detonation up the silo stack and a 30-minute radiation field centred on the wreck. §8Hazmat counters the field; a config option can disable it.§r\n\n§5§lDECAY §lHEAT§r\nEvery shutdown leaves it: §9twenty minutes of mandatory cooling water§r, out of the §9same Feedwater hatch§r the running plant drank from. It is deferred, never waived - dismantling the silo does not cancel the bill.\n§1It takes every fluid the running draw takes, worst rung first§r - §8plain Water, Distilled Water, IC2 Coolant, then Grades 1 to 8 Purified Water§r - so a plant plumbed for ONE grade of purified water and nothing else can still pay its shutdown.\n\n§5§lCOOLING §lTOWERS§r\nTwo 17x17x20 hyperboloids on the platform strip to your LEFT as you face the silo, raised by the same projection. Per standing tower, up to two: feedwater draw §2x0.5§r, passive heat decay §2x2§r, decay-heat demand §2x0.5§r.\n\n§5§lSEIZURE§r\nA different failure entirely: coolant starvation at speed. The interlock and the protective spin-down make it hard to reach now, but a chamber already near SCRAM can still tear the spine\u0027s rotor housings apart and slam the plant shut.\n\n§5§lWHAT §lSURVIVES§r\n- The §9Nuclear Plant Foundation§r is blast-proof: it holds your whole campaign record, so no explosion takes it. Every other block breaks like any GregTech casing.\n- Breaking a §9Reactor Fuel Pillar Frame§r that still holds rods drops the rods on the ground. Nothing is lost.\n- §9Over-injection:§r hand the output hatches more EU than they can take and the plant explodes, like any GregTech generator. To test a hatch row safely, an operator runs §9/btssafety on§r beside the controller: the excess is clamped away and every panel prints the shortfall and which row came up short. §9/btssafety off§r arms it again.\n\n§5§lDO §lTHIS§r\nWear a full hazmat suit near a running plant, and keep a water supply that survives your own shutdown.\n\n§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r\nA full hazmat suit - helmet, chestplate, leggings and Rubber Boots - is on you at once.\n\n§8Near a running plant, wear it: radiation does not care what is in your backpack. The quest reads your ARMOUR slots as well as your pack, so the suit you are wearing completes it.§r\n\n[warn]The plant is generous with power and unforgiving with physics.[/warn]",
